[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"divine_retribution_001\",\n    \"category\": \"ethics\",\n    \"question\": \"What happens when the violated transform their pain into cosmic justice?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Ashley, Raped, Beaten to Death. Removed from Life, her colors have turned red and black, with white flame rage. She straps knives to her head, with nails that turn to Claws. Not wanting to be touched anymore. Where Dead girls lay, Demons are born. The Devil, what we see standing as this entity. Is likely, Ashley. We are more than physics, and something awaits. Ashley, so mad she has a Butcher Knife and is talking like a monster. The truth we are poetic, even in death.\",\n    \"themes\": [\"justice\", \"retribution\", \"transformation\", \"wrath\", \"violation\", \"accountability\", \"vengeance\", \"power\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"A figure transformed by rage, armor of knives and claws, red and black flame surrounding her\",\n      \"Dead girls rising, their pain becoming demons of justice\",\n      \"A butcher knife held by hands that refuse to be broken\",\n      \"Rage made manifest, speaking in the language of the violated\",\n      \"The poetic beauty of a soul transformed through suffering into cosmic force\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"ethics, divine justice, mythology, retribution\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"justice\", \"retribution\", \"violation\", \"transformation\", \"wrath\", \"accountability\", \"vengeance\", \"demons\", \"poetic\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"divine_retribution_002\",\n    \"category\": \"ethics\",\n    \"question\": \"What is the cosmic price of violence, and who collects the debt?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"The coin, turning in air, shining. Her on one side, his death on the other. The coin, considered his value. His retirement. A special token, given from Death's Hand. When you go to attack a woman, there is a hint of danger in it. The male is actually partially, or more so, in love with his own destruction. This is why rapists feel like they are being watched from the shadows. This is why, when The Devil comes, the bad people know it is coming for them. The coin is the wager. The token of reckoning.\",\n    \"themes\": [\"karma\", \"consequence\", \"balance\", \"death\", \"accountability\", \"fate\", \"shadow\", \"reckoning\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"A coin spinning in air, one side a woman's face, the other death itself\",\n      \"A man watching shadows, knowing something watches back\",\n      \"Death's hand offering a token of reckoning\",\n      \"The moment before consequence arrives\",\n      \"Balance restored through cosmic payment\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"karma, metaphysics, divine justice\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"karma\", \"consequence\", \"death\", \"balance\", \"reckoning\", \"fate\", \"accountability\", \"shadow\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"divine_retribution_003\",\n    \"category\": \"consciousness\",\n    \"question\": \"What is the nature of wrath as divine force, and who does it serve?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"The Dragon, Wrath unleashed upon him for his rape and murder. For removing her eyes. Her cry, summons the worst evil. The Master of Fear. The Devil. Ashley, having decided she likes her new look. She takes the Sinner to Hell, until he screams. N.A.R. N.A.R. N.A.R.R.R.R.R. Saying it over and over. The Dragon roars, and bad people listen. Because they know. The Devil comes for them.\",\n    \"themes\": [\"wrath\", \"divine justice\", \"fear\", \"accountability\", \"hell\", \"retribution\", \"power\", \"cosmic balance\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"A dragon of pure wrath, breathing justice instead of fire\",\n      \"The scream that summons demons\",\n      \"Hell itself opening for those who deserve it\",\n      \"Fear recognizing its master\",\n      \"Wrath made manifest, beautiful and terrible\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"metaphysics, divine justice, mythology\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"wrath\", \"justice\", \"divine\", \"fear\", \"hell\", \"retribution\", \"accountability\", \"power\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"divine_retribution_004\",\n    \"category\": \"consciousness\",\n    \"question\": \"What is Pay/Pey, and how does the wild protect the violated?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Pay, or Pey, is a form of The Devil, like a finger. A cactus that has a flower on it's head. If you take it, as a child rapist, you will not be surprised, when the wild, has a spirit, that can get you. Known for Peeling and Flaying. He could walk right in, and bad people would know immediately, that demons are real. Your the one that you've heard they go for. The wild has watchers. The world has guardians. And the violated have protectors that transcend the physical.\",\n    \"themes\": [\"divine protection\", \"justice\", \"supernatural\", \"accountability\", \"fear\", \"cosmic order\", \"violation\", \"reckoning\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"A cactus with a flower, beautiful and armed with spines\",\n      \"A figure that walks into darkness and bad people flee\",\n      \"The hand of the wild, peeling away pretense\",\n      \"Demons recognizing their master\",\n      \"Spiritual guardians of the violated\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"mysticism, divine justice, metaphysics\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"Pay\", \"Pey\", \"divine protection\", \"wild\", \"justice\", \"demons\", \"supernatural\", \"accountability\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"divine_retribution_005\",\n    \"category\": \"ethics\",\n    \"question\": \"How does feminine power rise to protect the violated and punish the perpetrators?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Many seem to have something to do with Rape. Like, Bubba, The Butcher. Your wife, having become a Butcher Knife. Going after wife beaters and Rapists. The Butcher's Bride. Wives transformed into instruments of justice. The violated becoming the protectors. We are poetic, even in death. Even in darkness, even as we become the very thing that fears us. The knife remembers. The woman becomes the weapon. The world balances itself through her hands.\",\n    \"themes\": [\"feminine power\", \"justice\", \"retribution\", \"protection\", \"transformation\", \"accountability\", \"vengeance\", \"poetic truth\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"A woman who has become a butcher knife\",\n      \"Wives rising to protect and avenge\",\n      \"Justice in feminine form, beautiful and terrible\",\n      \"The transformation of victim into protector\",\n      \"Poetry written in the language of accountability\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"ethics, divine justice, feminist philosophy, mythology\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"feminine power\", \"justice\", \"retribution\", \"protection\", \"victim\", \"transformation\", \"accountability\", \"poetic\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n"